SUBENT        C0481001   20260818   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                  7         17
TITLE      Cross sections relevant to gamma-ray astronomy:
           Proton induced reactions
AUTHOR     (P.Dyer,D.Bodansky,A.G.Seamster,E.B.Norman,
           D.R.Maxson)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,23,1865,1981)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.23.1865
INSTITUTE  (1USAWAU,1USAMSU,1USABRN)
FACILITY   (VDGT,1USAWAU) The University of Washington three-
            stage tandem Van de Graaff accelerator.
DETECTOR   (GELI) Two Ge(Li) detectors: 47 mm in diameter by 54
            mm long and 42 mm in diameter by 39 mm long.
HISTORY    (19990413C)
           (20010307A) Date on ENTRY and SUBENT records corrected.
           (20200506A) OS. REACTIONs corrected in subs.2-20
           (20260818A) BP: Added subentries 22-34, replaced
           NACRE data with a digitized data set in subentry 21,
           updated STATUS.
ENDBIB              17
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           20
SUBENT        C0481002   20260818   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                  5         17
REACTION   (6-C-12(P,X)6-C-12,PAR/CUM,SIG,G,AV)
            Beta decay included.
SAMPLE     Natural carbon target with thickness
            1.8 (0.1) mg/cm**2.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Errors arise from
            - errors in yield extraction (larger
              at the higher photon energies)          5 %;
            - beam current integration                3 %;
            - target thickness measurement       5 - 13 %;
            - Ge(Li) efficiency measurement:
              - for low-energy gamma rays             5 %
              - for 4.44- and 6.13-MeV gamma rays    10 %
             are added quadratically to give the approximate
             absolute errors given.
STATUS     (TABLE,,P.Dyer+,J,PR/C,23,1865,1981) Table - 2
HISTORY    (20200506A) REACTION SF7=G added
           (20260818A) BP: Updated STATUS.
ENDBIB              17
